Feature: Automate migration of files from S3 landing folder to archive folder

  Background:
    Given the Databricks secret scope "aws_keys" contains "access_key" and "secret_key"
    And the Unity Catalog is set to "purgo_databricks"
    And the Unity Catalog Schema is set to "purgo_playground"

  Scenario: Migrate files with SUCCESS status
    Given the s3_file_process_log table contains files with file_status "SUCCESS"
    When the script reads the s3_landing_path and s3_archive_path for each file
    Then the file should be moved from the landing folder to the archive folder
    And the operation should be logged in the s3_file_transfer_audit table

  Scenario: Handle files with non-SUCCESS status
    Given the s3_file_process_log table contains files with file_status not equal to "SUCCESS"
    When the script processes the files
    Then the files should not be moved
    And an error message "File status not eligible for archiving" should be logged

  Scenario Outline: Validate file paths and credentials
    Given the s3_file_process_log table contains a file with <file_status>
    And the s3_landing_path is "<s3_landing_path>"
    And the s3_archive_path is "<s3_archive_path>"
    When the script attempts to move the file
    Then the operation should <result>
    And the log should contain "<log_message>"

    Examples:
      | file_status | s3_landing_path                                      | s3_archive_path                                      | result          | log_message                              |
      | SUCCESS     | s3://agilisium-playground-dev/filestore/purgo/source | s3://agilisium-playground-dev/filestore/purgo/target | succeed         | "File moved successfully"                |
      | FAILED      | s3://agilisium-playground-dev/filestore/purgo/source | s3://agilisium-playground-dev/filestore/purgo/target | not succeed     | "File status not eligible for archiving" |
      | SUCCESS     | invalid_path                                         | s3://agilisium-playground-dev/filestore/purgo/target | not succeed     | "Invalid landing path"                   |
      | SUCCESS     | s3://agilisium-playground-dev/filestore/purgo/source | invalid_path                                         | not succeed     | "Invalid archive path"                   |

  Scenario: Error handling for missing credentials
    Given the Databricks secret scope "aws_keys" does not contain "access_key" or "secret_key"
    When the script attempts to access S3
    Then an error message "Missing AWS credentials" should be logged

  Scenario: Log file transfer audit
    Given a file is successfully moved from landing to archive
    When the operation is completed
    Then the s3_file_transfer_audit table should be updated with the run_start_time and run_end_time
